{"availability":"available","full":"koji-1009/paging_view","name":"paging_view","description":"Like Android Jetpack's Paging library 3, manages data and displays paged lists.","category":"Other","language":"Dart","stars":8,"forks":2,"created":"2022-07-18T06:24:07Z","updated":"2026-09-30T23:54:31Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://koji-1009.github.io/paging_view/","topics":["dart","flutter","paging"],"demo":"https://koji-1009.github.io/paging_view/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T00:29:20.853Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T00:29:20.853Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T00:29:20.853Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T00:29:20.853Z","stars":8,"forks":2}],"technologies":["Flutter"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["pagingview is a robust Flutter library for managing and displaying paginated data. Inspired by Android Jetpack's Paging library, it adopts a DataSource-driven architecture, enabling a clear separation between your data loading logic and the UI.","Whether you are building a simple infinite scroll list, a complex grid, a grouped list, or a sophisticated sliver-based layout, pagingview provides a type-safe and flexible foundation."],"features":["Separation of Concerns: Defines data loading logic in a dedicated DataSource class, keeping your Widgets clean, focused, and testable.","Real-time Data Updates: DataSource allows dynamic updateItem, updateItems, insertItem, and removeItem operations for seamless UI synchronization.","PagingList, PagingGrid: High-level widgets for common use cases.","SliverPagingList, SliverPagingGrid: For use in a CustomScrollView to create sophisticated scroll effects (e.g., with an SliverAppBar).","Grouped Lists: Built-in support for GroupedPagingList and GroupedPagingGrid, making it easy to render sectioned data (e.g., by date or category) with sticky headers."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/koji-1009/paging_view/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"c821356515558ad60f996